<newsitem itemid="173862" id="root" date="1996-11-07" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: London Insurance Market H1 profits rise.</title>
<headline>London Insurance Market H1 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		2.16		  vs 1.70</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.75		  vs 1.10</p>
<p> Pretax		     7.6		   vs 6.0</p>
<p> Investment income	8.5		   vs 7.1</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.07		  vs 0.06</p>
<p> Tax			  1.5		   vs 1.2</p>
<p> Net taxed		  6.0		   vs 4.8</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 31, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - London Insurance Market Investment Trust Plc (LIMIT) is an investment fund participating in the Lloyd's of London insurance market on a limited liability basis.</p>
<p>NOTE - LIMIT said it expected a return of about 7.0 percent on its 1995 capacity after deducting its special central fund contribution and a return of 8.5 percent on its 1994 capacity.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
